“Middleware is a component in the .NET Core request-response pipeline that processes incoming HTTP requests and outgoing HTTP responses.

Each middleware can inspect, modify, or handle the request. It can also pass the request to the next middleware component.

Examples include authentication, authorization, exception handling, logging, and CORS.

Middleware execution depends on the order in which it is registered in Program.cs.”
Important interview question
What is the difference between app.Use(), app.Run(), and app.Map()?
- app.Use() → Can call the next middleware.
- app.Run() → Terminal middleware; does not call the next middleware.
- app.Map() → Creates a branch in the pipeline based on a matching path.
